From 866d3f083deb3242ce8998065f76b116586eefee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:43:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] zeo_i18n: Spanish (es) -- Zed's strings and Zeo's own screens
 (pilot)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The first language after pt-BR, as a pilot for the other six: locales/es/ holds
zed-core.ftl (5,706 of Zed's 5,905 strings, command-palette action names included) and
the ten files of Zeo's own screens (370 messages). Drafted with Lara (no_trace) without
the "imperative" instruction that ruined pt-BR's drafts -- 48-71% of the drafts kept per
batch -- and revised by hand; not reviewed by a native speaker. Neutral Spanish for Spain
and Latin America, tú where a form of address cannot be avoided; "jail", "sandbox" and
"thread" stay English.

Ungrouped and made of new files only, so it applies under any USE set. The screen files
come whole, unlike pt-BR's, which each screen patch carries: in a build without a group
the messages of that group's screens ship unused, which costs nothing at run time; the
full tree (test.sh) is where i18n-check compares them with en-US.
---

